\begin{align*}
M_x &= \frac{Q_x + R_x}{2} = \frac{-15 + 1}{2} = -7 \\
M_y &= \frac{Q_y + R_y}{2} = \frac{-19 - 7}{2} = -13
\end{align*}
So, $M = (-7, -13)$. The slope of the line $PM$ is:
\begin{align*}
m_{PM} &= \frac{M_y - P_y}{M_x - P_x} = \frac{-13 - 5}{-7 + 8} = -18
\end{align*}
Using the point-slope form of the line equation, we have $y - 5 = -18(x + 8)$. Simplifying, we get $y = -18x - 142$. Since $x + 2y + c = 0$, comparing coefficients, we have $a = 1$ and $c = 142$. Therefore, $a + c = \boxed{143}$. </think> <answer>$143$</answer>

